lean-units
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Project:   lean-units - https://github.com/ecyrbe/lean-units
  Version:   commit 5322fc77dd4e3ec8d31af2c757a47abbeb94d500
  Licence:   MIT License, Copyright 2025 ecyrbe
  Vendored:  lean/vendor/lean-units/, unmodified

lean-units is a physical-units system for Lean 4: a dimension is a product of
base dimensions raised to rational powers, and a unit is a choice of metric in a
dimension. The calculus in `docs/src/calculus/` is written against it, which is
why it is vendored rather than fetched - a dimension system whose meaning can
change under a build is not one a proof should rest on.

The files under `LeanUnits/`, and `LeanUnits.lean`, `lakefile.toml`,
`lean-toolchain`, `lake-manifest.json` and `LICENSE`, are copied unmodified.
`Examples/` and `.github/` are not taken, because nothing here builds them. The
full MIT text is in `lean/vendor/lean-units/LICENSE` and is not reproduced here.

Its own formal-proof side is incomplete upstream, so this development treats it
as a definitions library: the dimension and unit structures, and the
`auto_dim`/`auto_equiv` tactics. Nothing here is proved by appealing to one of
its theorems, and `Azoth/Axioms.lean` enforces that automatically by reporting
the transitive axiom set of every theorem this project claims.

